# Cloudflare Pages headers config (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/).
#
# This site changes multiple times a day and doesn't get heavy traffic --
# freshness matters a lot more than shaving a revalidation round-trip off
# page loads. no-cache still lets the browser cache a response, it just
# forces a conditional revalidation (If-None-Match against the ETag) on
# every load instead of trusting a max-age window blindly. Real bug this
# fixes: the previous default (Cloudflare Pages' own max-age=14400) meant
# a returning maintainer could load stale JS for up to 4 hours after a
# deploy with zero indication anything was wrong -- reported directly as
# "Vivaldi won't let go of this old site" even after manually clearing
# site data, which only clears storage, not the browser's own HTTP cache.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
